    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-363" contextRef="c-45">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;1)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 8.71pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;2)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 8.71pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;3)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 8.71pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;4)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 8.71pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;5)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 8.71pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-365" contextRef="c-45">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal; font-size: small; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: small; text-align: inherit; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: normal; font-size: small; background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: small; text-align: inherit; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1" style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Enterprise TE Products Pipeline Company LLC (&amp;quot;TE Products&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;Company&amp;quot;) is a Texas limited liability company and an indirect wholly owned subsidiary of Enterprise Products Operating LLC, a Texas limited liability company (&amp;quot;EPOLLC&amp;quot;). EPOLLC in turn is wholly owned by Enterprise Products Partners L.P., a Delaware limited partnership, which is a publicly traded partnership. EPOLLC is the operator of TE Products.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;TE Products owns and/or leases one of the largest refined products and LPG common carrier pipeline systems in the United States. This pipeline system is approximately 4,700 miles in length, extending from southeast Texas through the central and midwestern United States to the northeastern United States and includes the ATEX and Aegis pipeline systems mentioned below.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;The products pipeline system transports refined products from the Texas Gulf Coast, eastern Texas and southern Arkansas to the Central and Midwest regions of the United States with deliveries in Texas, Louisiana, Arkansas, Missouri, Illinois, Kentucky and Indiana. The products pipeline system transports LPGs from the Texas Gulf Coast to the Central, Midwest and Northeast regions of the United States and is the only pipeline that transports LPGs from the Texas Gulf Coast to the Northeast. The products pipeline system east of Todhunter near Middleton, Ohio, is devoted solely to the transportation of LPGs. The products pipeline system also transports normal butane and isobutane to the Midwest for use in the production of motor gasoline and transports natural gasoline/diluent for use in the North.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;The 1,300-mile ATEX pipeline system originates in Washington County, Pennsylvania and is connected to four fractionators in the Marcellus/Utica Shale region. These plants include the MarkWest Houston plant in Pennsylvania and the MarkWest Cadiz plant in Ohio, the Blue Racer Natrium plant in West Virginia and the Utica East Ohio Scio plant in Ohio.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;The pipeline system transports ethane from these origin points to Mont Belvieu, Texas.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;TE Products delivers ethane between the Mont Belvieu storage complex and Napoleonville, Louisiana on the Aegis Ethane Pipeline system (or &amp;quot;Aegis&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC. Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; Property, plant and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Revenues are earned from transportation of refined products, LPGs, and ethane, sale of product inventory and other ancillary services. Transportation revenues are recognized as products are delivered to customers. Revenues from the sale of product inventory are recognized when the products are sold.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;During 2025, TE Products rebilled shippers for under-recovery resulting from the vacated January 20, 2022 rehearing order (Docket No. RM20-14-001) in the amount of $29,649,498.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; (See Commission's order issued on November 20, 2025 (Docket No. RM93-11-003, paragraph 37, footnote 111)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;These revenues are reported in account 645 &amp;quot;Unusual or Infrequent Items (credit)&amp;quot; on page 114.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;TE Products is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the Company to EPOLLC and, with the exception of the Texas Franchise Tax, if applicable, does not recognize this liability on the Company's financial statements. For purposes of calculating income taxes for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report), TE Products employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;TE Products does not have any employees. The Company's management and administrative and operating functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company on behalf of EPOLLC, the Operator. The Company reimburses EPOLLC for the allocated costs of Enterprise Products Company employees who perform operating, management and other administrative functions for the Company under the terms of an operating agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small"&gt;&lt;br style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
